Kind: ablation
Issue: #951
Takes out: the boot as a job waited for -- it runs in the foreground again, as before #951, and a shell runs a trap only once the command it waits for in the foreground has ended: the merge test sent SIGTERM during its boot lets that boot run to its end, judges it as any other, and never says it was stopped.  harness-lifecycle-check.sh's mtstop finds no line saying the boot was stopped, and the run saying it stopped after its last boot instead of at boot 1 of 1.
Script: scripts/harness-lifecycle-check.sh
Script: --only
Script: mtstop
Expect: lifecycle: mtstop: .* -- WRONG
Note: run under each accelerator ablate.sh is given, which passes --kvm to harness-lifecycle-check.sh under KVM

